# Keep a native scan open during comparison

An optional **Open CT/MRI (new tab)** link sits beside existing guided-step and
selected-structure modality links. The normal same-tab links and existing inline
3D Atlas comparison are retained. This is not a new default navigation mode or
an automatic pop-up.

The optional action uses a canonical, revision-bound concept or complete guided
step and opens a new tab with `noopener noreferrer`. Unknown, stale, partial,
foreign and private query fields do not create an action. MRI-only concepts do
not acquire CT targets. An unavailable local guided mask can still have its
existing canonical destination; the destination checks its own availability.

The current study, slice, overlays and unanswered practice stay in their own
tab. No files, handles, patient coordinates, crosshairs, answer state, entitlement
or approval are transferred by this link. The new tab follows normal sign-in,
access and approved-source selection. A configured local preview may open its
existing approved source; otherwise select the approved folder there.

These are separate, unregistered CT/MRI subjects. This feature adds no spatial
synchronization, registration, segmentation, case publication or clinical
approval. It changes neither accepted masks nor the desktop clinical PACS.
No new package, media, font, dataset, service, licence obligation or fee.

Local isolated candidate only. Refer to its current source-bound checkpoint for
tests, browser evidence and installation status; source availability is not a
deployment or signed-in/acquired-study acceptance claim.
